From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:05:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Book ABI: select the deployed original book's actual ABI by
 exact code hash; no pendingOwner

Root's live preflight failed: eth_call execution reverted. Root's read-check
(custody-v2-live-20261023/evidence/book-abi-readcheck.json) shows that the deployed
book 0xe4f570e9 has no pendingOwner() selector. That book is the first,
single-step-owner EnclaveAddressBook: Projects/enclave 6c1135b0f, reproduced byte for
byte offline with that commit's settings (solc 0.8.35, runs 200; 1809 bytes, keccak
e4f570e9). The source, ABI, runtime, a reproduce script and provenance are in
evidence/book-legacy.

activation.mjs:
- BOOK_ABIS is keyed by exact code hash; any other book code refuses;
- the pendingOwner read and check are removed (the book has no pending-owner state);
- the strict owner and code pins stay;
- every failed eth_call names the method, contract and provider.

The test fake's book code is the actual deployed runtime. It answers only selectors
dispatched by that bytecode and declared in its ABI; others revert. A test checks the
selectors against root's live evidence.

Counterexample: the previous activation.mjs (24aac73), run against this fixture,
refuses with 'eth_call: execution reverted' (root's live failure); the fix prepares.

activation 11/11 (256 MiB), browser 3/3 (512 MiB). Nothing was served or signed.
